    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2AT2cnGhUcR1SQd8fnQL6FF)_\n\n## What\nHovering over an Org `[cite:@key]` link now shows the full formatted reference, as in Obsidian's Pandoc Reference List. It lives in `sp-citations` (the bibliography files are registered by `sp-bibprocess`; the rendering uses `citar`).\n\n- **Tooltip**: a `help-echo` on the link, shown when the mouse rests on it.\n- **Echo area**: an Eldoc function, shown when point is on the link.\n- `sp-cite-hover-display` (default `(tooltip echo)`) picks either, both or neither.\n- The text is the `preview` template of `citar-templates`, so changing that template changes the hover text. With several keys, the one under the mouse or point is shown (the first on the prefix/suffix). A missing key shows `@key: not found in the bibliography`.\n\nDocs: new \"Citation hover\" section in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org`; the `.el` is tangled from it (tangling also removed some trailing whitespace in untouched lines of `sp-citations.el`). CHANGELOG entry added under Open pull requests.\n\n## Tested\nEmacs 29.3 in batch with `citar` stubbed: key lookup, tooltip function, missing key, outside a link, and the Eldoc callback.\n\n## Not tested\nReal `citar`, a real tooltip on the Mac, and Eldoc in the interactive config.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAf2qqyk9d5s2KU3g7)_",
